WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:06.030
Donald Trump's disapproval has exploded in
the last two weeks and there seem to be two

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:07.590
big factors.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:13.089
Number one, Trump's just tragically, historically
disastrous response to the recent mass shootings.

00:00:13.089 --> 00:00:18.380
Uh, and then in addition to that, you've got
the continued recession fears and stock market

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:19.380
crashes.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.090
800 points lost on the dowel yesterday.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:22.960
More than a 3% decline there.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:27.830
And on the Nasdaq and on the s and p 500 and
Donald Trump just continues to tweet nonsense

00:00:27.830 --> 00:00:30.849
about the economy and about trade and about
who's to blame.

00:00:30.849 --> 00:00:37.450
And the most amazing thing about all of this
is that a Fox News poll finds that Trump is

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:38.930
really not doing well.

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:44.399
Fox just released a presidential approval
poll, which has trumpet 56% disapproval.

00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:52.109
Now, before I go any further, it's shocking
that it's only 56% in other words, the fact

00:00:52.109 --> 00:00:58.649
that only 56% of the country disapproves of
the job Trump is doing is a real red flag

00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:01.539
about tens of millions of people in our country.

00:01:01.539 --> 00:01:07.370
But needless to say, this has now basically
tied to the record for the highest Trump disapproval.

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:09.480
The point here is the trendline.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:12.440
Trump's disapproval is up five full points
from last month.

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:17.660
And again, it's back to essentially statistically
matching the record high disapproval Trump

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:23.290
has had during his presidency, which was October
of 2017 nearly two years ago.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:27.740
And the timing of this from an electorial
perspective could be good as we start to get

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.710
into the 2020 election in full.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:35.880
And meanwhile, Donald Trump continues to do
nothing substantive, uh, about, uh, economic

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.520
policy obviously because he doesn't understand
it.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:43.000
He continues to do nothing substantive about
the gun violence issues in the United States.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:48.360
And the same Fox News poll found that two
thirds of Americans, this is a significant

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.200
majority in such a hyper-partisan environment.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:56.360
Two thirds of Americans want a ban on assault
rifles and semiautomatic weapons.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:02:00.320
This is up seven points over the last 15 or
so months.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.180
This is a very important change.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:04.810
We already knew background checks were popular.

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:10.530
The Fox News poll finds that there is 90%
support for universal background checks, criminal

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.920
background checks on every gun, purchase and
sale.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:21.250
Uh, however it is across party lines, 90%
of Democrats want universal background checks.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:24.420
90% of Republicans want universal background
checks.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:27.140
This is not common in the United States.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:31.190
So listen, um, it's clear why Trump's approval
is dropping.

00:02:31.190 --> 00:02:33.060
You have mat mass violence events.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:39.030
When Barack Obama presided over mass violence
events, he would empathize with the victims

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:40.130
in a genuine way.

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:42.750
It's not that much to ask for, but he did
it.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:47.400
Donald Trump attacks political opponents doubles
down on bad ideas.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:53.470
Take smiling, thumbs up pictures with a baby
just orphaned by the mass shooting.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:54.670
So it makes sense.

00:02:54.670 --> 00:03:00.020
But even still, even though the trend line
is going towards disapproval, how does 40%

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:03.330
of the countries still approve of the job
this man is doing?

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:08.930
How does nearly a third of the country think
that Donald Trump's actions are pulling the

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:09.930
country together?

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:13.930
When the obvious a reality is the opposite
of that?

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:20.470
How clueless do you have to be to look at
what's going on and come away with that opinion?

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:23.330
So at the micro level, can we just pass background
checks?

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:25.610
I mean, 90% of the country wants them.

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:28.240
Can we just get it done at the macro level?

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.500
We see all of this data.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:31.570
We see Trump's disapproval climbing.

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:36.069
We see Trump's polling underwater in a bunch
of swing states for the 2020 election.

00:03:36.069 --> 00:03:41.360
Bernie Biden, Warren, all polling ahead of
Trump and hypothetical matchups, but are we

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.780
going to remove him or are we going to blow
it?

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:44.959
That's my question.

